WEBVTT

00:00:00.139 --> 00:00:02.300
You know, for a first take, I think it

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.540
went pretty well. We had things moving

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:07.179
in real time, calling back to our main

00:00:07.179 --> 00:00:09.980
hub system, actively reporting on our

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.140
mobile device. It was uh it was pretty

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:14.779
good. Uh and here we&#x27;re seeing sort of a

00:00:14.779 --> 00:00:17.180
take two. We&#x27;re going up a level. uh

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.340
we&#x27;re adding a device into the ecosystem

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.500
basically trying to see in what way

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.980
shape or form can we communicate or uh

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.620
add extra communication uh to our talks

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.020
by having a simple watch device which

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.300
everybody&#x27;s using. So uh today we&#x27;re not

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.940
only taking a look at the nature of

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:38.539
privacy 3D printing curation and control

00:00:38.539 --> 00:00:40.219
uh but we&#x27;re also taking a stab at our

00:00:40.219 --> 00:00:43.660
own demo of uh open source technology.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:45.820
So, couldn&#x27;t think of a better place to

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:47.260
talk to people about what they think,

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.020
what motivates them, what got them to

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.219
stand up, uh, but also test some stuff

00:00:52.219 --> 00:00:54.699
out, see what people think. So, uh,

00:00:54.699 --> 00:00:55.700
let&#x27;s check it out. All right. So, today
